Keep the wide-char trail flag out of validateCell's hands.

A double-width character is one glyph in two cells: TText::drawStr writes it
into the first and marks the second with TScreenCharacter::fTrail. A trail
cell's text is a single '\0', and DisplayBuffer::validateCell turns any cell
whose first byte is '\0' into a space -- initWithChar, which zeroes _flags and
so takes the trail marking with it. The flush algorithm then reaches the second
cell of every wide character, finds no trail, and on a platform where
wideOverlapping is true (every unix) writes the space over it. A real terminal
answers a write into the right half of a double-width character by blanking
both halves, so the character disappears: `[A メモ한 B]` is drawn as
`[A      B]`, with the six columns still reserved.

Reproduced at ee11435 (2026-08-30) with a plain TApplication drawing
TDrawBuffer::moveStr("[A" "メモ한" "B]") -- no Gren, no node -- captured with
tmux capture-pane. A regression in d726902 (2026-07-06): d726902^ draws it,
d726902 does not, both built and run.

Reported as magiblot/tvision#233. Delete this file when it is fixed upstream;
build-tvision.sh will skip a patch that no longer applies and say so.

